---
// S2 Why a new firm, margin label. Desktop 128:3555, mobile 128:6413.
import '@fontsource/schibsted-grotesk/latin-400.css';
import Ruler from './Ruler.astro';
const tick = 'rgba(8,29,94,.35)';
---
<section aria-labelledby="wwa-why" class="relative bg-white" data-node="128:3555" data-node-m="128:6413">
  <Ruler dir="down" color={tick} class="hidden lg:block absolute left-0 top-0 w-full h-[12px]" node="128:3717" />
  <Ruler dir="up" color={tick} class="lg:hidden absolute left-0 bottom-[4px] w-full h-[12px]" nodeM="128:6469" />
  <div class="relative max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-[20px] lg:px-[80px] pt-[60px] pb-[72px] lg:pt-[112px] lg:pb-[80px] lg:flex">
    <div class="relative flex items-start lg:block lg:w-[264px] lg:pt-[8px] lg:shrink-0">
      <div class="w-[52px] shrink-0 pt-[4px] lg:w-auto lg:pt-0"><p class="m-0 w-max tm-label lg:t-label text-navy lg:text-royal whitespace-nowrap" data-node="128:3718" data-node-m="128:6414">01</p></div>
      <p class="m-0 w-max tm-body-strong lg:t-body-strong text-ink lg:w-auto lg:mt-[10px]" data-node="128:3719" data-node-m="128:6415">Why a new firm</p>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute left-0 right-0 top-[36px] lg:static lg:block lg:mt-[16px] lg:w-[264px] h-px bg-line lg:bg-navy/40" data-node="128:3720" data-node-m="128:6416"></span>
    </div>
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="hidden lg:block w-px self-stretch bg-line ml-[72px] mt-[8px] shrink-0" data-node="128:3721"></span>
    <div class="relative mt-[42px] pl-[32px] lg:mt-0 lg:pl-0 lg:ml-[47px] lg:min-w-0 lg:-mr-[16px]">
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="lg:hidden absolute left-0 top-0 w-[2px] h-full bg-royal" data-node-m="128:6418"></span>
      <h2 id="wwa-why" class="m-0 tm-h2 lg:t-h2 text-navy" data-node="128:3722" data-node-m="128:6417">Same Experience. A New Way.</h2>
      <p class="bs-wnudge m-0 mt-[16px] lg:mt-[24px] font-display font-normal text-ink text-[22px] leading-[32px] lg:text-[28px] lg:leading-[40px] lg:tracking-[-0.15px] lg:w-[752px] lg:max-w-full">We left a legacy firm to build something leaner, more responsive, and focused only on you, without the bureaucracy that slows claims down.</p>
      <p class="m-0 mt-[20px] lg:mt-[28px] tm-body lg:t-lead text-ink lg:w-[720px] lg:max-w-full">Michael Rapport was a top producer at one of the nation's leading public adjusting firms, across hundreds of losses. He left to run claims the way he thought they should run: fewer files, a senior adjuster on each one, and the same person from the first call to the settlement.</p>
      <p class="m-0 mt-[16px] lg:mt-[20px] tm-body lg:t-lead text-ink lg:w-[720px] lg:max-w-full">That is Blue Star Adjusters. A boutique firm, with its head office in Sacramento.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
